  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 16 January 1928; the four retiring councillors were returned unopposed (Mid-Ulster Mail, 7 January 1928, p. 5). 'There were four vacancies, and for these the retiring Councillors were nominated. Their names are — Mr. J. D. Anderson ... Mr. Richard Charles, Mr. Wm. M'Clay and Mr. Wm. H. Newell. There will not be any contest.' Returned unopposed."
